<?xml version="1.0"?>
<psalm
    errorLevel="1"
    resolveFromConfigFile="true"
    findUnusedBaselineEntry="true"
    findUnusedCode="false"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns="https://getpsalm.org/schema/config"
    xsi:schemaLocation="https://getpsalm.org/schema/config vendor/vimeo/psalm/config.xsd"
>
    <!-- S444 — the production corpus (src + scripts) back at errorLevel 1.

         S306 widened THIS single config to cover tests/ and pinned the shared
         errorLevel to 5 so the test tree could join without a baseline. The
         cost was silent, because errorLevel is per-config, not per-directory:
         src/ and scripts/ — clean at level 1 before S306, the "Psalm 1 green"
         AGENTS.md still advertises — quietly relaxed to level 5, four tiers of
         issue types in production code no longer failing CI even though the
         directory list here still named them. (psalm 6.5.0, the pinned
         analyser, has no per-directory level: the pre-Psalm-3 <levels> element
         is absent from vendor/vimeo/psalm/config.xsd, verified by schema
         inspection — so the strictness split has to be a config split.)

         The arrangement now:
           * THIS file         — src + scripts at errorLevel 1 (production, strict);
           * psalm-tests.xml   — tests/ at the measured errorLevel 5; S306's ladder
                                 evidence and the level rationale live there,
                                 verbatim-preserved.

         CI runs BOTH as separate steps in the Psalm job — "Run Psalm (src +
         scripts at L1)" and "Run Psalm (tests at L5)" — each failing the build
         on its own. Tests reference src classes; psalm READS those files for
         cross-boundary inference under psalm-tests.xml but reports findings
         there only for files in that config's corpus, never double-reporting a
         src issue at the test-tree level.

         No psalm-baseline.xml, no <IssueHandler> suppressions, and this file
         carries zero <file> exclusions — the whole documented exclusion
         corpus of the hub is one written-why entry, the S332 cross-repo route
         dumper, and it belongs to psalm-tests.xml alone (it lives under
         tests/). Fix findings at the source; a suppression here would
         reproduce the "gate that proves nothing" defect S146 removed.

         Scope is asserted by tests/Unit/Support/StaticAnalysisScopeTest.php:
         deleting either config file, dropping a <directory> entry, mutating a
         CI command line (including silently repointing the tests step back at
         this config), or relaxing either errorLevel reddens the suite, not
         just the psalm job.

         The venue PHP is 8.3.6 (Psalm needs >= 8.3.16 to boot), so CI's
         "Psalm Static Analysis" check is the authoritative verdict for this
         tree; the sandbox reproduction is the s306-style docker mirror —
         php 8.3.33 + swoole 6.2.2 + pcntl/posix/pdo_mysql, no php-ast. -->
    <projectFiles>
        <directory name="src"/>
        <directory name="scripts"/>
        <ignoreFiles>
            <directory name="vendor"/>
        </ignoreFiles>
    </projectFiles>
</psalm>
